          "anonymized": false,
          "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/a96149971e91f0ceb638e9e86cef2b08.gif",
          "created": "2018-04-09T03:11:40.225Z",
          "name": "Tupper - VRChat Head of Community",
          "serviceAccount": false,
          "urlName": null
        }
      ],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "5e9fdc03d19e806812655430",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5cdd1a9a0f4d2d0bf789f4f5",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 8
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Final IK is still required for IK related things. The main thing that constraints replaced was the things we were doing with rigid bodies, fixed joints, and the VRC IK Follower. \nRight now I wouldn't really recommend using Final IK for simple things like moving items around the avatar (gun from hip to hand), or pointing something at something else, but you can't replace the more complicated things like VRIK or the Grounders of Final IK.\nConstraints are incredibly nice, but still act as a band-aide to the underlying problem of not being able to directly reference bones in the humanoid armature. Honestly, due to constraints stability, it's not as big of an issue as it used to be.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
