      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ec57cf2ccc4cb75017a91b8|full_name}: Using rigid bodies for world fixed objects means you can suffer from stutter. Lindesu made a prefab and video on how to use constraints for world fixed objects that is very stable:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T1U9E_TdcYQ&feature=youtu.be\nIt uses negative values to basically do the opposite of what you do, keeping it in place.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
